{"$schema":"https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"artifacts":[{"contents":{"text":"<scxml xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml\" version=\"1.0\" datamodel=\"ecmascript\" initial=\"a\">\n  <datamodel>\n    <data id=\"retry-count\" expr=\"0\"/>\n    <data id=\"class\" expr=\"'gold'\"/>\n    <data id=\"max.tries\" expr=\"3\"/>\n    <data id=\"_total\" expr=\"0\"/>\n  </datamodel>\n  <state id=\"a\">\n    <transition event=\"fail\" cond=\"retry-count &lt; 3\" target=\"a\">\n      <assign location=\"retry-count\" expr=\"retry-count + 1\"/>\n      <log label=\"retry\" expr=\"'attempt ' + retry-count\"/>\n    </transition>\n    <transition event=\"fail\" target=\"b\"/>\n  </state>\n  <final id=\"b\"/>\n</scxml>\n"},"location":{"uri":"tests/ui/lint015-ecmascript-data-id.scx"},"mimeType":"application/scxml+xml"}],"columnKind":"utf16CodeUnits","properties":{"diagnosticCounts":{"errors":1,"notes":0,"total":5,"warnings":4},"producer":{"kind":"validator"}},"results":[{"fixes":[{"artifactChanges":[{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/lint015-ecmascript-data-id.scx"},"replacements":[{"deletedRegion":{"byteLength":11,"byteOffset":125,"endColumn":26,"endLine":3,"startColumn":15,"startLine":3},"insertedContent":{"text":"retryCount"}},{"deletedRegion":{"byteLength":11,"byteOffset":322,"endColumn":47,"endLine":9,"startColumn":36,"startLine":9},"insertedContent":{"text":"retryCount"}},{"deletedRegion":{"byteLength":11,"byteOffset":378,"endColumn":36,"endLine":10,"startColumn":25,"startLine":10},"insertedContent":{"text":"retryCount"}},{"deletedRegion":{"byteLength":11,"byteOffset":397,"endColumn":55,"endLine":10,"startColumn":44,"startLine":10},"insertedContent":{"text":"retryCount"}},{"deletedRegion":{"byteLength":11,"byteOffset":460,"endColumn":56,"endLine":11,"startColumn":45,"startLine":11},"insertedContent":{"text":"retryCount"}}]}],"description":{"text":"rename the variable to `retryCount` here and in 4 references"},"properties":{"applicability":"maybe-incorrect"}}],"level":"warning","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/lint015-ecmascript-data-id.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":26,"endLine":3,"startColumn":15,"startLine":3}}}],"message":{"markdown":"`retry-count` is not an ECMAScript identifier: it contains `-`\n\n**Note:** the ECMAScript data model creates this variable (SCXML 1.0 §B.2.1) as a property of the global object, reachable only as `globalThis['retry-count']`; `retry-count` in an expression is not this variable: `-` subtracts, so `retry-count` reads two variables\n\n**Help:** to use the variable in expressions, name it with an identifier that is also an XML ID, such as `retryCount`, and rename every reference to it\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §5.3 <data>\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §B.2 The ECMAScript Data Model","text":"`retry-count` is not an ECMAScript identifier: it contains `-`"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":136,"start":125},"category":"lint"},"relatedLocations":[{"id":1,"message":{"text":"`retry-count` is referenced here"},"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/lint015-ecmascript-data-id.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":47,"endLine":9,"startColumn":36,"startLine":9}}}],"ruleId":"LINT015"},{"fixes":[{"artifactChanges":[{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/lint015-ecmascript-data-id.scx"},"replacements":[{"deletedRegion":{"byteLength":5,"byteOffset":163,"endColumn":20,"endLine":4,"startColumn":15,"startLine":4},"insertedContent":{"text":"classValue"}}]}],"description":{"text":"rename the variable to `classValue`"},"properties":{"applicability":"maybe-incorrect"}}],"level":"warning","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/lint015-ecmascript-data-id.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":20,"endLine":4,"startColumn":15,"startLine":4}}}],"message":{"markdown":"`class` is an ECMAScript reserved word, not an identifier\n\n**Note:** the ECMAScript data model creates this variable (SCXML 1.0 §B.2.1) as a property of the global object, reachable only as `globalThis['class']`; no expression or `<assign location>` can name it directly\n\n**Help:** to use the variable in expressions, name it with an identifier that is also an XML ID, such as `classValue`, and rename every reference to it\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §5.3 <data>\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §B.2 The ECMAScript Data Model","text":"`class` is an ECMAScript reserved word, not an identifier"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":168,"start":163},"category":"lint"},"ruleId":"LINT015"},{"fixes":[{"artifactChanges":[{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/lint015-ecmascript-data-id.scx"},"replacements":[{"deletedRegion":{"byteLength":9,"byteOffset":200,"endColumn":24,"endLine":5,"startColumn":15,"startLine":5},"insertedContent":{"text":"maxTries"}}]}],"description":{"text":"rename the variable to `maxTries`"},"properties":{"applicability":"maybe-incorrect"}}],"level":"warning","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/lint015-ecmascript-data-id.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":24,"endLine":5,"startColumn":15,"startLine":5}}}],"message":{"markdown":"`max.tries` is not an ECMAScript identifier: it contains `.`\n\n**Note:** the ECMAScript data model creates this variable (SCXML 1.0 §B.2.1) as a property of the global object, reachable only as `globalThis['max.tries']`; `max.tries` in an expression is a property access, not this variable\n\n**Help:** to use the variable in expressions, name it with an identifier that is also an XML ID, such as `maxTries`, and rename every reference to it\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §5.3 <data>\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §B.2 The ECMAScript Data Model","text":"`max.tries` is not an ECMAScript identifier: it contains `.`"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":209,"start":200},"category":"lint"},"ruleId":"LINT015"},{"fixes":[{"artifactChanges":[{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/lint015-ecmascript-data-id.scx"},"replacements":[{"deletedRegion":{"byteLength":6,"byteOffset":236,"endColumn":21,"endLine":6,"startColumn":15,"startLine":6},"insertedContent":{"text":"total"}}]}],"description":{"text":"rename the declaration to `total`"},"properties":{"applicability":"maybe-incorrect"}}],"level":"error","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/lint015-ecmascript-data-id.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":21,"endLine":6,"startColumn":15,"startLine":6}}}],"message":{"markdown":"`<data id>` `_total` begins with `_`\n\n**Note:** SCXML reserves names that begin with `_` for system variables such as `_event`, `_sessionid`, `_name`, and `_ioprocessors`, and a conformant document declares no data with such an id\n\n**Help:** rename the data without the leading `_`, and update every reference to it\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §5.10 System Variables","text":"`<data id>` `_total` begins with `_`"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":242,"start":236},"category":"semantic"},"ruleId":"SCXML073"},{"level":"warning","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/lint015-ecmascript-data-id.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":36,"endLine":10,"startColumn":25,"startLine":10}}}],"message":{"markdown":"`location` is not an assignable ecmascript location: `retry-count` is not an ECMAScript variable name\n\n**Note:** a location expression must name a place in the data model that can be assigned, such as a variable name or a property access like `a.b` or `a[0]`\n\n**Help:** `<data id=\"retry-count\">` declares a variable no ECMAScript expression can name (`LINT015`): rename it, for example to `retryCount`, in its declaration and every reference\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §5.9.2 Location Expressions\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §B.2 The ECMAScript Data Model","text":"`location` is not an assignable ecmascript location: `retry-count` is not an ECMAScript variable name"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":389,"start":378},"category":"lint"},"relatedLocations":[{"id":1,"message":{"text":"declared here with a name that is not a variable name"},"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/lint015-ecmascript-data-id.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":26,"endLine":3,"startColumn":15,"startLine":3}}}],"ruleId":"SCXML039"}],"tool":{"driver":{"informationUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/","name":"scxml-validator","rules":[{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"SCXML 1.0 §B.2.1: \"the SCXML Processor MUST create an ECMAScript variable object whose name is the value of the 'id' attribute of <data>\", and an XML ID such as `retry-count`, `max.tries`, or `class` is conformant (§5.10 reserves only a leading `_`, `SCXML073`), so the data model creates the variable as a property of the global object; but it is reachable only as `globalThis['retry-count']`, and a reference such as `retry-count < 3` parses as something else (it subtracts `count` from `retry`)"},"help":{"text":"How to fix: to use the variable in expressions, rename it to an identifier such as `retryCount` in its declaration and every reference (the finding offers the rename).\n\nSpecification: SCXML 1.0 §B.2 The ECMAScript Data Model\n\nRun `scx --explain LINT015` for examples."},"helpUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/#ecma-profile","id":"LINT015","name":"LINT015","properties":{"category":"lint"},"shortDescription":{"text":"an ECMAScript `<data id>` is not an identifier, so no expression can name it"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"`location`, `idlocation`, `namelist` items, and `<foreach item/index>` must name an assignable place; SCXML 1.0 defines the run-time outcome of one that does not, so the document compiles: §5.9.2 \"If a location expression cannot be evaluated to yield a valid location, the SCXML processor MUST place the error 'error.execution' in the internal event queue\", and §4.6 \"if 'item' does not specify a legal variable name, the SCXML processor MUST terminate execution of the <foreach> element and the block that contains it, and place the error error.execution on the internal event queue\". In ECMAScript an assignable place is a variable or a property access such as `data.field` or `data[0]`; in XPath it is an expression that selects existing nodes, such as `$data` or `$data/field` (`a.b` is one variable name containing a dot, and `a[0]` is a predicate)"},"help":{"text":"How to fix: ECMAScript: use a variable name or a member expression such as `data.field`; XPath: use a `$`-rooted path to a declared variable such as `$data/field`.\n\nSpecification: SCXML 1.0 §5.9.2 Location Expressions\n\nRun `scx --explain SCXML039` for examples."},"helpUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/#LocationExpressions","id":"SCXML039","name":"SCXML039","properties":{"category":"semantic"},"shortDescription":{"text":"a location is not assignable in the selected data model"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"SCXML 1.0 §5.10: \"Variable names beginning with '_' are reserved for system use. A conformant SCXML document MUST NOT contain ids beginning with '_' in the <data> element.\" (under the null data model `<data>` itself is `SCXML037`)"},"help":{"text":"How to fix: rename the data without the leading `_`, and update every reference to it.\n\nSpecification: SCXML 1.0 §5.10 System Variables\n\nRun `scx --explain SCXML073` for examples."},"helpUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/#SystemVariables","id":"SCXML073","name":"SCXML073","properties":{"category":"semantic"},"shortDescription":{"text":"a `<data id>` begins with `_`"}}],"semanticVersion":"0.2.0"}}}],"version":"2.1.0"}